WEBVTT

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:30.440
are as varied as the number
of people in this room.

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:32.896
So imagine that.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:36.896
This color that we've all been
taught since kindergarten is primary --

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:38.496
red, yellow, blue --

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:40.896
in fact is not primary,

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:42.696
is not irreducible,

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:46.680
is not objective but quite subjective.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:48.696
What?

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:50.336
(Laughter)

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:52.880
Albers called this "relational."

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:55.800
Relational.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:57.896
And so it was the first time

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:03.200
that I was able to see my own neighborhood
as a relational context.